    <text><list><item>Medication: stopped, Oxycodone 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet every 6 hours as needed for pain, no more than four a day (60 MME a day) [S]</item><item>Medication: started, Oxycodone 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet three times daily as needed for pain [S]</item><item>Medication: started, Oxycodone 5 mg oral tablet, one tablet at bedtime as needed for pain [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Duloxetine 60 mg delayed-release oral capsule, one capsule daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Acetaminophen 500 mg oral tablet, two tablets three times daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Diclofenac sodium 1% topical gel, 2 g to the right ankle four times daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Cholecalciferol (vitamin D3) 2,000 units oral tablet, one tablet daily [S]</item><item>Goal: Improve the PEG score by at least 30% from baseline. In progress; target 2026-10-29 [S]</item><item>Goal: Stand at the easel for 30 minutes at a time by the six-week review. In progress; target 2026-10-29 [S]</item><item>Goal: First opioid dose reduction, agreed by the patient, without loss of function. In progress; target 2026-10-29 [S]</item><item>Goal: Naloxone in the home with a family member trained to use it. Outcome by 2026-09-17: Naloxone nasal spray dispensed; spouse taught at the first visit [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 2026-09-17 [S]</item><item>Next visit 2026-10-29: six-week chronic pain review of function, mood, and the opioid taper [S]</item></list></text>

